          "uco-observable:strings": [
            {
              "@id": "urn:uuid:b985e08a-76d9-58c2-a487-532903ea15b5",
              "@type": "uco-observable:ExtractedString",
              "uco-observable:stringValue": "Case 1:24-cr-00227-PTG Document 1 Filed 10/24/24 Page 1 of 10 PageID# 1\n\nFILED\nIN OPEN COURT\n\nIN THE UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT FOR THE\niHJ 2 4\nEASTERN DISTRICT OF VIRGINIA\nCLERK U.S. DISTRICT COURT\nALEXANDRIA. VIRGINIA\nAlexandria Division\n\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA UNDER SEAL\n\nV.\nCase No. l:24-CR-227\n\nCount 1: 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251(a) and (e)\nCASH TAYLOR DALTON,\nAttempted Sexual Exploitation of Children\na/lc/a \u201ccashdalton23\u201d, a/k/a\nContacUaylor321 @gmail.com. a/k/a Count 2: 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2422(b)\ncontacttavlordalton@mnail.coin Coercion and Enticement of a Minor to Engage in\nIllegal Sexual Activity\n\nDefendant. Count 3: 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2252(a)(2) and (b)(1)\nAttempted Receipt of Child Pornography\n\nForfeiture Notice\n\nINDICTMENT\n\nOctober 2024 Term\u2014at Alexandria, Virginia\nCOUNT ONE\n(Attempted Sexual Exploitation of Children)\nTHE GRAND JURY CHARGES THAT:\n\nBetween on or about and betw'een July 1, 2023 to October 30, 2023, within the Eastern\n\nDistrict of Virginia and elsewhere, the defendant, CASH TAYLOR DALTON, \u201dcashdalton23.\n\na/k/a Contacttaylor321@gmail.com, a/k/a contacttaylordalton@gmal I.com attempted to employ,\n\nuse, persuade, induce, entice, and coerce a minor (age 12), Minor 1, to engage in sexually explicit\n\nconduct for the purpose of producing a visual depiction of such conduct, and such visual depictions\n\nwere produced and transmitted using materials that have been mailed, shipped, and transported in\n\nand affecting interstate and foreign commerce by any means, and had actually been transported\n\nand transmitted using any means and facility of interstate and foreign commerce and in and\n\naffecting interstate and foreign commerce.\n\n(All in violation of Title 18, U.S. Code, Section 2251(a) and (e).)\nCase 1:24-cr-00227-PTG Document 1 Filed 10/24/24 Page 2 of 10 PageID# 2\n\nCOUNT TWO\n(Coercion and Enticement of a Minor to Engage in Illegal Sexual Activity)\n\nTHE GRAND JURY FURTHER CHARGES THAT:\n\nBetween on or about July 1, 2023 to October 30, 2023, within the Eastern District of\n\nVirginia and elsewhere, the defendant, CASH TAYLOR DALTON, cashdalton23,\u201d a/k/a\n\nContacttaylor321@gmaii.com, a/k/a contacttaylordalton@gmail.com using a facility and means\n\nof interstate and foreign commerce, did knowingly persuade, induce, entice, and coerce an\n\nindividual who had not attained the age of 18 years, Minor 1 (age 12), to engage in sexual activity\n\nfor which any person can be charged with a criminal offense, including, Code of Virginia Sections\n\n18.2-370 (taking indecent liberties with children), 18.2-374.1:1 (distribution and solicitation of\n\nchild pornography), and 18.2-374.3 (use of a communications systems to facilitate certain offenses\n\ninvolving children), and did knowingly attempt to do so.\n\n(All in violation of Title 18, U.S. Code, Section 2422(b).)\nCase 1:24-cr-00227-PTG Document 1 Filed 10/24/24 Page 3 of 10 PageID# 3\n\nCOUNT THREE\n(Attempted Receipt of Child Pornography)\n\nTHE GRAND JURY FURTHER CHARGES THAT:\n\nBetween on or about July 1, 2023 to October 30, 2023, within the Eastern District of\n\nVirginia and elsewhere, the defendant, CASH TAYLOR DALTON, cashdalton23,\u201d a/k/a\n\nContacttaylor321@gmail.com, a/k/a contacttaylordalton@gmail.com did knowingly attempt to\n\nreceive a visual depiction using a means and facility of interstate and foreign commerce, and which\n\nvisual depiction had been transported in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce, by any\n\nmeans including by computer, and the production of such visual depiction involved the use of a\n\nminor engaging in sexually explicit conduct and the visual depiction was of such conduct.\n\n(All in violation of Title 18, U.S. Code, Section 2252(a)(2) and (b)(1).)\nCase 1:24-cr-00227-PTG Document 1 Filed 10/24/24 Page 4 of 10 PageID# 4\n\nFORFEITURE NOTICE\n\nTHE GRAND JURY FURTHER FINDS THAT:\n\nThe defendant, CASH TAYLOR DALTON, cashdalton23\u201d, a/k/a\n\nContacttaylor321@gmail.com, a/k/a contacttaylordalton@gmail.com is hereby notified, pursuant\n\nto Federal Rule of Criminal Procedure 32.2(a), that upon conviction of Counts One and Three of\n\nthis Indictment, he shall forfeit to the United States: (1) any visual depiction described in 18 U.S.C.\n\n\u00a7\u00a7 2251, 2251 A, 2252, 2252A, 2252B, or 2260, and any matter that contains any such visual\n\ndepiction, which was produced, transported, mailed, shipped, and received in violation of this\n\nchapter; (2) any property, real or personal, constituting or traceable to gross profits or other\n\nproceeds obtained from such offenses; and (3) any property, real or personal, used or intended to\n\nbe used to commit or to promote the commission of the offense, and any property traceable to such\n\nproperty.\n\nThe defendant, CASH TAYLOR DALTON, cashdalton23\u201d, a/k/a\n\nContacttaylor321@gmail.com, a/k/a contacttaylordalton@gmail.com is hereby notified, pursuant\n\nto Federal Rule of Criminal Procedure 32.2(a), that upon conviction of Count Two of the\n\nIndictment, the defendant shall forfeit to the United States, pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2428(a): (1)\n\nthe defendant's interest in any property, real or personal, constituting or derived from any proceeds\n\nhe obtained, directly or indirectly, as a result of such violation; and (2) the defendant\u2019s interest in\n\nany property, real or personal, that was used or intended to be used to commit or to facilitate the\n\ncommission of such violation.\n\nThe property subject to forfeiture includes, but is not limited to, the following:\n\n(1) One (1) Space Grey MacBook Serial #C02F5o6LML86;\n(2) One (1) Black iPhone model A1661 with brown clear case;\n(3) One (1) Silver MacBook Serial #W892451 W66D;\n(4) One (1) Silver MacBook Air Serial # FVFYP3YALYWJ.\nCase 1:24-cr-00227-PTG Document 1 Filed 10/24/24 Page 5 of 10 PageID# 5\n\nIf any property subject to forfeiture is unavailable, the United States may seek an order\n\nforfeiting substitute assets pursuant to Title 21, U.S. Code, Section 853(p) and Federal Rule of\n\nCriminal Procedure 32.2(e).\n\n(All in accordance with Title 18, United States Code, Sections 2253 and 2428(a);\nTitle 21, United States Code, Section 853(p); and Fed. R. Crim. P. 32.2.)\n\nA TRUE BILL\nJESSICA D. ABER\n\u25a0P\nUnited States Attorney\n;-GovernmentAct,\nTtie original of this page has been filed\nBy: ' r\nunder seal in the Clerk\u2019s Office\nAlessandraP. Serano\nAssistant United States Attorney\nCase 1:24-cr-00227-PTG Document 1 Filed 10/24/24 Page 6 of 10 PageID# 6\n\nFILEO\nIN OPEN COURT\n\nIN THE UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT FOR THE\nh;F 2 4\nEASTERN DISTRICT OF VIRGINIA\nCLERK U.S. DISTRICT COURT\nALEXANDRIA, VIRGINIA\nAlexandria Division\n\nUNITED STATES OF AMERICA UNDER SEAL\n\nV.\nCase No. U24-CR-227\n\nCount I: 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2251 (a) and (e)\nCASH TAYLOR DALTON,\nAttempted Sexual Exploitation of Children\na/k/a \u201ccashdalton23\u201d, a/k/a\nContacttavlor321 ,@gmail.com. a/k/a Count 2: 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2422(b)\ncontacttavlordalton@,ginai 1 .com Coercion and Enticement of a Minor to Engage in\nIllegal Sexual Activity\n\nDefendant. Counts: 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2252(a)(2) and (b)(1)\nAttempted Receipt of Child Pornography\n\nForfeiture Notice\n\nINDICTMENT\n\nOctober 2024 Term\u2014at Alexandria, Virginia\nCOUNT ONE\n(Attempted Sexual Exploitation of Children)\nTHE GRAND JURY CHARGES THAT:\n\nBetween on or about and between July 1, 2023 to October 30, 2023, within the Eastern\n\nDistrict of Virginia and elsewhere, the defendant, CASH TAYLOR DALTON, \u201ccashdalton23,\n\na/k/a Contacttaylor321@gmail.com, a/k/a contacttaylordalton@gmai l.com attempted to employ,\n\nuse, persuade, induce, entice, and coerce a minor (age 12), Minor 1, to engage in sexually explicit\n\nconduct for the purpose of producing a visual depiction of such conduct, and such visual depictions\n\nwere produced and transmitted using materials that have been mailed, shipped, and transported in\n\nand affecting interstate and foreign commerce by any means, and had actually been transported\n\nand transmitted using any means and facility of interstate and foreign commerce and in and\n\naffecting interstate and foreign commerce.\n\n(All in violation of Title 18, U.S. Code, Section 2251(a) and (e).)\nCase 1:24-cr-00227-PTG Document 1 Filed 10/24/24 Page 7 of 10 PageID# 7\n\nCOUNT TWO\n(Coercion and Enticement of a Minor to Engage in Illegal Sexual Activity)\n\nTHE GRAND JURY FURTHER CHARGES THAT:\n\nBetween on or about July 1, 2023 to October 30, 2023, within the Eastern District of\n\nVirginia and elsewhere, the defendant, CASH TAYLOR DALTON, cashdalton23,\u201d a/k/a\n\nContacttaylor321@gmail.com, a/k/a contacttaylordalton@gmail.com using a facility and means\n\nof interstate and foreign commerce, did knowingly persuade, induce, entice, and coerce an\n\nindividual who had not attained the age of 18 years, Minor 1 (age 12), to engage in sexual activity\n\nfor which any person can be charged with a criminal offense, including, Code of Virginia Sections\n\n18.2-370 (taking indecent liberties with children), 18.2-374.1:1 (distribution and solicitation of\n\nchild pornography), and 18.2-374.3 (use of a communications systems to facilitate certain offenses\n\ninvolving children), and did knowingly attempt to do so.\n\n(All in violation of Title 18, U.S. Code, Section 2422(b).)\nCase 1:24-cr-00227-PTG Document 1 Filed 10/24/24 Page 8 of 10 PageID# 8\n\nCOUNT THREE\n(Attempted Receipt of Child Pornography)\n\nTHE GRAND JURY FURTHER CHARGES THAT:\n\nBetween on or about July 1, 2023 to October 30, 2023, within the Eastern District of\n\nVirginia and elsewhere, the defendant, CASH TAYLOR DALTON, cashdalton23,\u201d a/k/a\n\nContacttaylor321@gmail.com, a/k/a contacttaylordalton@gmail.com did knowingly attempt to\n\nreceive a visual depiction using a means and facility of interstate and foreign commerce, and which\n\nvisual depiction had been transported in and affecting interstate and foreign commerce, by any\n\nmeans including by computer, and the production of such visual depiction involved the use of a\n\nminor engaging in sexually explicit conduct and the visual depiction was of such conduct.\n\n(All in violation of Title 18, U.S. Code, Section 2252(a)(2) and (b)(1).)\nCase 1:24-cr-00227-PTG Document 1 Filed 10/24/24 Page 9 of 10 PageID# 9\n\nFORFEITURE NOTICE\n\nTHE GRAND JURY FURTHER FINDS THAT:\n\nThe defendant, CASH TAYLOR DALTON, cashdalton23\u201d, a/k/a\n\nContacttayIor321@gmail.com, a/k/a contacttaylordalton@gmail.com is hereby notified, pursuant\n\nto Federal Rule of Criminal Procedure 32.2(a), that upon conviction of Counts One and Three of\n\nthis Indictment, he shall forfeitto the United States: (1) any visual depiction described in 18 U.S.C.\n\n\u00a7\u00a7 2251, 2251 A, 2252, 2252A, 2252B, or 2260, and any matter that contains any such visual\n\ndepiction, which was produced, transported, mailed, shipped, and received in violation of this\n\nchapter; (2) any property, real or personal, constituting or traceable to gross profits or other\n\nproceeds obtained from such offenses; and (3) any property, real or personal, used or intended to\n\nbe used to commit or to promote the commission of the offense, and any property traceable to such\n\nproperty.\n\nThe defendant. CASH TAYLOR DALTON, cashdalton23\u201d, a/k/a\n\nContacttaylor321@gmail.com, a/k/a contacttaylordalton@gmail.com is hereby notified, pursuant\n\nto Federal Rule of Criminal Procedure 32.2(a), that upon conviction of Count Two of the\n\nIndictment, the defendant shall forfeit to the United States, pursuant to 18 U.S.C. \u00a7 2428(a): (1)\n\nthe defendant\u2019s interest in any property, real or personal, constituting or derived from any proceeds\n\nhe obtained, directly or indirectly, as a result of such violation; and (2) the defendant\u2019s interest in\n\nany property, real or personal, that was used or intended to be used to commit or to facilitate the\n\ncommission of such violation.\n\nThe property subject to forfeiture includes, but is not limited to, the following:\n\n(1) One (1) Space Grey MacBook Serial #C02F5o6LML86;\n(2) One (1) Black iPhone model A1661 with brown clear case;\n(3) One (1) Silver MacBook Serial #W892451W66D;\n(4) One (1) Silver MacBook Air Serial # FVFYP3YALYWJ.\nCase 1:24-cr-00227-PTG Document 1 Filed 10/24/24 Page 10 of 10 PageID# 10\n\nIf any property subject to forfeiture is unavailable, the United States may seek an order\n\nforfeiting substitute assets pursuant to Title 21, U.S. Code, Section 853(p) and Federal Rule of\n\nCriminal Procedure 32.2(e).\n\n(All in accordance with Title 18, United States Code, Sections 2253 and 2428(a);\nTitle 21, United States Code, Section 853(p); and Fed. R. Crirn. P. 32.2.)\n\nA TRUE BILL\nJESSICA D.ABER\np\nUnited States Attorney\n;-GovernmentAct,\nThe original of this page has been filed\nBy: under seal in the Clerk\u2019s Office\nAlessandra P. Serano\nAssistant United States Attorney"
